  "query": "For a real-time, horizontally scalable chat application designed to support millions of concurrent users (similar to Slack), what are the top 5 architectural strategies to achieve scalability and reliability?\n\nFor each strategy, provide 3 pros and 3 cons, and cover:\n        •        Cloud-Native vs. Platform-Agnostic deployment trade-offs (e.g., AWS/GCP/Azure managed services vs. portable, self-managed deployments).\n        •        Consistency Model Trade-offs: primarily targeting strong consistency but evaluating the operational and performance impacts if eventual consistency is accepted.\n        •        Scalability Mechanisms: partitioning, sharding, message fan-out, and storage optimizations.\n        •        Fault Tolerance & Latency: handling partial outages while keeping real-time delivery guarantees.\n\nThe evaluation should be language-agnostic, focusing on architectural principles rather than specific programming languages, but may reference widely used technologies (e.g., Kafka, Redis, WebSockets, gRPC) as examples.\n\nTarget audience: college students in Computer Sciences and Engineering"
